<div class="whatsnew">
  <h3>What's new · version {{ release.version }} · {{ release.date }}</h3>
  <p class="small" style="margin:0 0 6px">One list for everything added since the first release, grouped by what it lets you do.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Choose targets with better evidence.</strong> Seven independent evidence streams (mutation recurrence, copy number that moves the gene product, DepMap dependency, TCGA-KIRC replication and survival, phosphosites turned into kinase activity, tumour purity) feed two separate scores, one for targets and one for biomarkers, each with a rank interval from 1,000 random re-weightings.</li>
    <li><strong>Trust the text.</strong> Every sentence the agents write is checked against the evidence it cites: the id must exist, belong to that gene, and the numbers and the up or down wording must match. A guard also fails any sentence whose evidence changed after the agents read it.</li>
    <li><strong>Predict treatment response.</strong> IMmotion150 (atezolizumab with or without bevacizumab against sunitinib) and the Choueiri 2016 nivolumab trial now give response and progression results per gene. Two published signatures reproduce, so the trial data work. No gene separates the two arms once 20,000 tests are corrected for.</li>
    <li><strong>Look inside the tumour.</strong> Tumours are split by VHL, PBRM1, BAP1 and SETD2 mutation and by ccA or ccB subtype. The ccA/ccB difference is also a component of the biomarker profile.</li>
    <li><strong>Judge antibody and radioligand targets.</strong> Surface proteins are ranked by topology, increase in tumour, staining in vital organs and how evenly tumour cells express them.</li>
    <li><strong>See the immune neighbourhood.</strong> CIBERSORT and xCell define cold, intermediate and hot tumours and feed an immune-target profile. A second single-cell dataset (Zhang 2021) checks the cell-type calls.</li>
    <li><strong>See the tissue.</strong> The new Tissue viewer draws spots on the real H&amp;E sections and shows the neighbours of any gene's high-expression spots.</li>
    <li><strong>Count prior work better.</strong> Literature counts use only aliases that belong to one gene, and ChEMBL potent compounds and patent records now reduce the "undrugged" credit.</li>
    <li><strong>One criterion changed after seeing data.</strong> A "selective dependency" now needs at least three dependent ccRCC cell lines (Chronos below -0.5). Before, one or two of 24 lines could carry the call. This is logged as a post-hoc change in <code>evals/history.md</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
